PointGrad-CAM (OpenPCDet / PointRCNN) — Per-detection Export + Metrics
=====================================================================

This pipeline generates Grad-CAM saliency for 3D point clouds using PointRCNN
(OpenPCDet). It computes per-detection object-level explanation maps and
evaluation metrics:

- Focus Ratio
- Sparsity@alpha
- Faithfulness ΔScore@alpha
- Deletion Curve + AUC


------------------------------------------------------------
1) Outputs (per sample)
------------------------------------------------------------

All outputs are written under:

    --outdir/sample_XXXXXX/

Files:
    metadata.json
    detections.csv
    metrics_summary.csv        (compatible with plot_xai_metrics.py)

Per detection:
    sample_XXXXXX/<ClassName>/detYYY_scoreZ/heatmap.npz
    (optional) heatmap.ply
    (optional) debug.npz

heatmap.npz contains:
    points          (N,3)
    scores          (N,)
    colors          (N,3)

And also includes the metric fields and deletion arrays:
    focus_ratio
    sparsity
    baseline_eval
    delta_s_alpha
    deletion_fracs
    deletion_scores
    deletion_auc


------------------------------------------------------------
2) Required input format
------------------------------------------------------------

Point cloud format:
    float32 (N,4) = (x, y, z, intensity)

Two supported input modes:

A) Raw single frame:
    Provide a KITTI velodyne .bin file using:
        --raw-bin /path/to/000062.bin

B) Dataset mode (recommended):
    Provide KITTI root and infos using the dataset loader (KittiZipDataset / KITTI folders).

Dataset mode expects:
    --kitti /path/to/KITTI
and that KITTI info files exist (recommended):
    /path/to/KITTI/Kitti_infos/kitti_infos_<split>.pkl


------------------------------------------------------------
3) YAML files needed
------------------------------------------------------------

Model YAML (required to build PointRCNN):
    tools/cfgs/kitti_models/pointrcnn.yaml

Dataset YAML (referenced by the model config):
    tools/cfgs/dataset_configs/kitti_dataset.yaml

Make sure in the dataset YAML:
- DATA_PATH points to your KITTI root (or is overridden by --kitti)
- INFO_PATH points to generated kitti_infos_*.pkl files
- DATA_SPLIT is correctly set for train/val/test


------------------------------------------------------------
4) Run (example)
------------------------------------------------------------

Example (dataset mode):

    python run_gradcam_metrics.py \
        --cfg tools/cfgs/kitti_models/pointrcnn.yaml \
        --ckpt checkpoints/pointrcnn_7870.pth \
        --kitti /path/to/KITTI \
        --sample 62 \
        --outdir /path/to/gradcam_results \
        --act-layer roi_head.merge_down_layer


------------------------------------------------------------
5) Paths you must update
------------------------------------------------------------

--cfg      : path to PointRCNN YAML config
--ckpt     : path to trained checkpoint (.pth)
--kitti    : KITTI dataset root directory
--outdir   : output folder where results will be written

If using raw frame mode:
--raw-bin  : path to a single KITTI velodyne .bin file


------------------------------------------------------------
6) Notes / Common pitfalls
------------------------------------------------------------

- This script runs the model on GPU (CUDA). Ensure torch.cuda.is_available() is True.
- Grad-CAM uses the specified activation layer (--act-layer). If the layer name is wrong,
  Grad-CAM will fail or output empty saliency.
- If baseline_eval becomes 0.0, strict matching failed for that detection during evaluation
  (often happens for unstable / low-score detections).
- Metrics are most stable when you keep:
  - fixed number of evaluation points (e.g., padding/downsampling deterministically)
  - strict matching settings consistent across methods

You are now ready to generate PointGrad-CAM explanations and metrics.
